WEBVTT

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:44.700
RAGE

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:30.700
All right, what should we order?

00:01:30.790 --> 00:01:31.870
Is offal stew okay?

00:01:32.160 --> 00:01:33.950
I've never had it.

00:01:34.040 --> 00:01:35.040
Seriously?

00:01:35.790 --> 00:01:36.790
Is it good?

00:01:37.120 --> 00:01:39.160
Yeah, I like it.

00:01:39.620 --> 00:01:41.080
Then I guess I'll give it a try.

00:01:41.660 --> 00:01:46.500
Okay, now all we need is
something light and refreshing.

00:01:51.620 --> 00:01:52.450
Hey.

00:01:52.750 --> 00:01:53.790
Yeah?

00:01:54.290 --> 00:01:57.700
You mentioned you used to be in a band.
You were on bass, right?

00:01:58.160 --> 00:02:01.910
Yeah, but only for a little while.

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:03.540
Do you still play?

00:02:04.500 --> 00:02:06.660
Yeah, sometimes. I have it back home.

00:02:07.160 --> 00:02:09.910
Is that so?

00:02:12.580 --> 00:02:15.040
I'd love to watch the next time you play.

00:02:25.160 --> 00:02:27.290
ACCOUNTING DEPARTMENT

00:02:44.790 --> 00:02:46.330
ARE YOU FREE?

00:02:53.370 --> 00:02:54.910
RAMEN TAIGA

00:02:55.000 --> 00:02:58.000
She said she wanted to see you play?

00:02:58.540 --> 00:03:00.450
What do you think it means?

00:03:00.540 --> 00:03:03.000
It just sounds
like she wants to go to your place.

00:03:04.870 --> 00:03:06.370
So that<i> was</i> it, then?

00:03:06.450 --> 00:03:08.080
Yeah, absolutely.

00:03:08.870 --> 00:03:10.950
Here you go, one miso ramen.

00:03:11.250 --> 00:03:13.370
So, what do you want?

00:03:14.370 --> 00:03:16.290
She's a nice girl, right?

00:03:19.250 --> 00:03:20.330
She is.

00:03:28.910 --> 00:03:31.250
OUTSKIRTS

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:33.870
Who here can play an instrument?

00:03:34.290 --> 00:03:35.700
An instrument?

00:03:36.660 --> 00:03:37.580
I play the recorder.

00:03:37.660 --> 00:03:39.330
-Castanets.
-Triangle.

00:03:41.620 --> 00:03:43.370
Who here can play an instrument?

00:03:43.450 --> 00:03:45.330
What does he want us to say?

00:03:45.410 --> 00:03:46.410
Don't know.

00:03:48.000 --> 00:03:49.660
I can play the piano if that helps.

00:03:52.540 --> 00:03:53.750
Dammit.

00:03:57.830 --> 00:03:58.950
Wha...

00:03:59.040 --> 00:04:00.660
What is this?

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:05.250
Did you really buy these without talking
to me, your accounting manager?

00:04:05.330 --> 00:04:07.790
What's done is done!

00:04:13.910 --> 00:04:15.870
You girls actually pull it off.

00:04:16.200 --> 00:04:17.620
Only the look.

00:04:17.700 --> 00:04:19.870
What's all this about?

00:04:20.450 --> 00:04:22.910
Do you know "Rockstock"?

00:04:23.410 --> 00:04:24.750
"Rockstock"?

00:04:26.200 --> 00:04:28.950
It's that kind of famous,
outdoor rock fest, right?

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:30.410
That's the one.

00:04:30.700 --> 00:04:35.200
Yesterday, I got an official offer
from the organizer asking us to perform.

00:04:36.250 --> 00:04:38.580
It seems a spot has suddenly opened up.

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:43.250
You're just there as a filler,
but I see it as our golden opportunity.

00:04:43.620 --> 00:04:46.200
For OTM Girls to take a leap forward,

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:48.580
we need a selling point
that others don't have.

00:04:49.790 --> 00:04:53.870
<i>If an underground idol group performed</i>
<i>as a band in a rock festival,</i>

00:04:53.950 --> 00:04:56.040
<i>don't you think it would create a buzz?</i>

00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:59.000
Only if we can actually play.

00:04:59.750 --> 00:05:02.200
Then see to it that you can.

00:05:02.290 --> 00:05:06.330
Like it's that easy. It takes years to--

00:05:06.410 --> 00:05:12.290
Starting today, we will begin preparing
for OTM Girls' rebirth as a band.

00:05:12.370 --> 00:05:15.160
Commit yourself to learning
your designated instrument.

00:05:16.000 --> 00:05:17.120
Heart and soul.

00:05:21.410 --> 00:05:24.830
We'd be better off practicing
how to dodge stones from the audience.

00:05:35.160 --> 00:05:39.830
"A chord consists of multiple notes
played at the same time."

00:05:41.080 --> 00:05:42.290
That's what it says.

00:05:42.700 --> 00:05:43.700
Right.

00:05:44.450 --> 00:05:45.910
First, put your middle finger here.

00:05:46.200 --> 00:05:47.370
Like this?

00:05:48.250 --> 00:05:49.950
And your ring finger here.

00:05:50.040 --> 00:05:53.040
Um, er... here?

00:05:53.290 --> 00:05:54.790
Then put your pinky here.

00:05:54.870 --> 00:05:55.750
That's impossible!

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:00.950
My fingers are killing me.
What chord is this?

00:06:01.370 --> 00:06:03.290
It's G, one of the easier chords.

00:06:03.370 --> 00:06:06.120
How? Was something overlooked
in the design process?

00:06:06.200 --> 00:06:07.750
Do you want to try playing?

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:08.950
Sure.

00:06:12.910 --> 00:06:13.830
I think it worked.

00:06:13.910 --> 00:06:16.830
No, I don't think it did.

00:06:19.870 --> 00:06:23.200
We always get bullied
into doing what Mr. Hyodo wants.

00:06:24.160 --> 00:06:25.790
We're used to it.

00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:27.580
I see.

00:06:28.080 --> 00:06:30.750
Although, when he said
he was making you the vocalist,

00:06:30.830 --> 00:06:32.910
I was having none of it.

00:06:35.830 --> 00:06:38.700
Don't take it seriously,
I was only joking.

00:06:41.330 --> 00:06:44.450
You must really hate
that I'm the vocalist.

00:06:44.750 --> 00:06:46.040
Of course I do.

00:06:47.750 --> 00:06:50.450
But we had no choice this time.

00:06:51.410 --> 00:06:52.410
I'm sorry.

00:06:56.910 --> 00:06:58.080
Hey.

00:06:59.250 --> 00:07:02.370
You think you can live a happy life
without hurting anyone, don't you?

00:07:05.700 --> 00:07:07.410
During a performance,

00:07:07.870 --> 00:07:10.450
there's you and there's the audience.

00:07:10.540 --> 00:07:12.750
<i>You become one with the atmosphere</i>

00:07:13.250 --> 00:07:17.160
and there's a moment when you feel
this thrill from head to toe.

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:19.120
You've felt it several times now, right?

00:07:21.830 --> 00:07:23.540
I can see it when I'm behind you.

00:07:25.410 --> 00:07:28.200
<i>So many people are drawn to your talent</i>

00:07:28.580 --> 00:07:30.870
<i>and you happily give them what they want.</i>

00:07:31.660 --> 00:07:33.080
That's enough.

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:34.330
Yeah.

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:36.790
So, stop apologizing.

00:07:38.080 --> 00:07:39.540
It's annoying, you know?

00:07:46.120 --> 00:07:48.080
Are you busy these days?

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:50.410
Yeah, well, the usual.

00:07:50.750 --> 00:07:51.870
I see.

00:07:56.000 --> 00:07:57.450
Have you talked to Retsuko recently?

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:59.290
A bit at the office.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:00.290
And?

00:08:00.370 --> 00:08:01.950
She's up to the usual.

00:08:04.580 --> 00:08:06.080
I see.

00:08:06.160 --> 00:08:09.500
So she's still performing
as an underground idol, per usual?

00:08:09.580 --> 00:08:10.410
What?

00:08:10.500 --> 00:08:15.080
She's become rather popular, hasn't she?
I hope she's enjoying it.

00:08:15.500 --> 00:08:16.660
Wait, you knew?

00:08:16.750 --> 00:08:18.370
Of course, I'm her friend.

00:08:18.450 --> 00:08:20.250
Oh my, so you knew all along.

00:08:21.200 --> 00:08:25.370
It seems she's started making money
so she can pay off her debts.

00:08:25.660 --> 00:08:28.750
Exactly. She's paying off her debts...

00:08:30.290 --> 00:08:31.700
Debts?

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:33.540
What?

00:08:34.250 --> 00:08:35.950
Was I not supposed to say that?

00:08:39.200 --> 00:08:41.330
We're going undercover at a concert.

00:08:41.750 --> 00:08:43.620
Huh? What's this all of a sudden?

00:08:43.700 --> 00:08:46.120
How can you remain calm
knowing she is in debt?

00:08:46.200 --> 00:08:49.000
There was a time
when she did seem to be struggling.

00:08:49.080 --> 00:08:51.620
Why didn't she come to me?

00:08:51.700 --> 00:08:53.950
I bet she didn't want you to worry.

00:08:54.040 --> 00:08:56.370
Do you have time today?
We should strategize.

00:08:56.450 --> 00:08:58.660
I can't today.

00:08:59.830 --> 00:09:01.250
I'm sorry.

00:09:01.330 --> 00:09:03.250
I have a prior engagement.

00:09:03.330 --> 00:09:05.700
Wait, you're meeting someone here?

00:09:06.750 --> 00:09:10.330
Oh well, I guess I have no other choice.

00:09:12.290 --> 00:09:13.620
Just 15 minutes of your time.

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:15.080
Why are you still here?

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:17.330
More importantly,
why the fancy private room?

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.580
Who's coming? A woman? It is, isn't it?

00:09:19.660 --> 00:09:21.330
Are you even listening to me?

00:09:25.580 --> 00:09:28.000
Sorry I'm late.

00:09:29.580 --> 00:09:30.660
Huh?

00:09:37.040 --> 00:09:38.750
<i>This is the C chord.</i>

00:09:41.410 --> 00:09:42.450
<i>This is D.</i>

00:09:44.370 --> 00:09:45.410
<i>This is E.</i>

00:09:48.370 --> 00:09:50.250
<i>This next one is the problem.</i>

00:09:50.540 --> 00:09:51.540
<i>F.</i>

00:09:53.410 --> 00:09:57.950
<i>The impregnable wall that stands before</i>
<i>all amateur guitarists.</i>

00:09:58.500 --> 00:10:02.700
<i>It's said this is where many challengers</i>
<i>fall to their knees in defeat.</i>

00:10:04.580 --> 00:10:08.910
<i>First, use your index finger to press down</i>
<i>strings one through six simultaneously.</i>

00:10:09.000 --> 00:10:10.500
<i>That is the first wall.</i>

00:10:11.410 --> 00:10:13.410
<i>Then, from this preposterous position,</i>

00:10:13.500 --> 00:10:15.830
<i>your remaining fingers go</i>
<i>here, here, and here.</i>

00:10:16.250 --> 00:10:17.580
<i>That is the second wall.</i>

00:10:17.910 --> 00:10:20.250
<i>If we were playing </i>Twister,
<i>it would look like this.</i>

00:10:25.790 --> 00:10:27.950
<i>Not even close.</i>

00:10:29.620 --> 00:10:31.540
I bet Inui is a nice girl.

00:10:31.620 --> 00:10:34.080
You should definitely date her.

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:35.540
Hey, are you listening?

00:10:35.620 --> 00:10:38.540
I'm listening.
You've told me that four times already.

00:10:38.620 --> 00:10:40.330
I have, have I?

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:45.410
An A-list celebrity.

00:10:45.950 --> 00:10:48.000
An unremarkable employee.

00:10:48.450 --> 00:10:52.540
When did you two hit it off?
You guys have nothing in common.

00:10:53.200 --> 00:10:55.040
We do, actually.

00:10:55.120 --> 00:10:56.830
Do tell.

00:10:59.040 --> 00:11:01.410
We were both turned down by Retsy.

00:11:03.450 --> 00:11:05.250
No way. You were dating?

00:11:05.500 --> 00:11:08.830
Goodness, no!
I just made my feelings known.

00:11:10.950 --> 00:11:12.870
Aw, come on.

00:11:12.950 --> 00:11:15.500
No wonder you flew
all the way to Hokkaido.

00:11:15.870 --> 00:11:18.120
Now that's genuine love.

00:11:18.200 --> 00:11:21.040
Hm, I see it now.

00:11:23.660 --> 00:11:25.250
But Haida...

00:11:28.080 --> 00:11:31.830
I'm not so sure
she's the girl you think she is.

00:11:33.910 --> 00:11:35.950
She's pretty complicated.

00:11:36.040 --> 00:11:38.580
Tadano, you know.

00:11:38.660 --> 00:11:42.160
Um, well, perhaps.

00:11:44.410 --> 00:11:47.910
She doesn't let people at work see it.

00:11:48.160 --> 00:11:51.620
Inui, was it? She seems genuine.

00:11:51.700 --> 00:11:54.540
I think she'd be good for you.

00:11:55.950 --> 00:11:57.290
It's hard, isn't it?

00:12:00.000 --> 00:12:00.870
Ta-da.

00:12:01.870 --> 00:12:02.950
What's that?

00:12:03.410 --> 00:12:05.830
I'm currently working
on a matchmaking app.

00:12:06.370 --> 00:12:08.750
Retsuko is registered, of course.

00:12:09.370 --> 00:12:12.290
Care to see if you're compatible?

00:12:14.830 --> 00:12:17.040
Nope. I'm good.

00:12:17.700 --> 00:12:20.620
What do you mean?
Geez, you're so difficult!

00:12:20.700 --> 00:12:22.290
Really, I'm good.

00:12:22.660 --> 00:12:23.950
Why not?

00:12:24.040 --> 00:12:25.620
I'm not into that kind of stuff.

00:12:25.700 --> 00:12:27.040
Just try it.

00:12:27.120 --> 00:12:28.750
I said I'm good.

00:12:28.830 --> 00:12:32.080
-But why not?
-You made that, Director Gori?

00:12:32.500 --> 00:12:33.620
Hm?

00:12:33.700 --> 00:12:36.620
That's amazing! May I see it as well?

00:12:36.700 --> 00:12:37.790
You're interested?

00:12:37.870 --> 00:12:38.700
I am.

00:12:38.790 --> 00:12:41.080
I'm so happy!

00:12:41.160 --> 00:12:43.580
So, where do I press?

00:12:43.660 --> 00:12:45.000
What you have to do...

00:12:49.120 --> 00:12:51.290
Ouch.

00:12:55.950 --> 00:12:57.410
I'm hungry.

00:13:02.080 --> 00:13:03.620
What are you doing?

00:13:03.700 --> 00:13:07.000
I gave you access rights to ENI-O
and renewed the algorithm.

00:13:07.500 --> 00:13:10.580
Now it will use
an AI analysis of users' history

00:13:10.660 --> 00:13:13.540
as a base to match up couples.

00:13:13.620 --> 00:13:15.000
Incredible!

00:13:15.330 --> 00:13:19.250
But isn't it expensive to use ENI-O?

00:13:19.580 --> 00:13:22.160
You let me tinker around,
so you don't have to pay.

00:13:22.250 --> 00:13:23.290
Really?

00:13:23.700 --> 00:13:26.040
I can help with server management too,
if you want.

00:13:26.120 --> 00:13:28.000
Running costs can be quite expensive.

00:13:28.450 --> 00:13:31.040
Yes, please!

00:13:34.450 --> 00:13:35.910
It's useless.

00:13:37.080 --> 00:13:40.200
It really is best to learn from someone
who knows what they're doing.

00:13:45.410 --> 00:13:47.910
<i>Do I know anyone</i>
<i>who can play an instrument?</i>

00:13:49.330 --> 00:13:50.950
<i>An instrumentalist...</i>

00:14:04.290 --> 00:14:05.250
<i>Hello?</i>

00:14:05.330 --> 00:14:08.080
Inui? Is this a good time?

00:14:08.540 --> 00:14:10.580
-Can we talk?
-<i>Yeah, it's all right.</i>

00:14:11.330 --> 00:14:12.580
<i>What's going on?</i>

00:14:12.660 --> 00:14:14.200
So...

00:14:15.580 --> 00:14:17.700
You said something
the other day, remember?

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.160
<i>Hm? What did I say?</i>

00:14:22.080 --> 00:14:24.580
That you want to see me play bass?

00:14:25.160 --> 00:14:26.950
<i>Ah!</i>

00:14:27.500 --> 00:14:28.790
I think I did say that.

00:14:30.410 --> 00:14:33.330
Um, so I was thinking...

00:14:40.410 --> 00:14:42.580
Wanna come over sometime?

00:15:11.370 --> 00:15:14.370
Subtitle translation by Rachel Momber
